#N canvas 40 60 1240 1010 the-gan 0;
#X text 20 10 THE GAN (Goodfellow et al. 2014): a GENERATOR mixes your favourites \, a CRITIC learns to tell your favourites from its mixes \, and each improves against the other. Everything is [expr] loops over arrays - open the boxes from top to bottom. One training step = [pd draw] (the dice) + [pd one-step] (pure arithmetic \, checked against numpy by dev/check.py)., f 168;
#N canvas 40 60 1240 900 critic 0;
#X text 20 10 THE CRITIC D judges the preset in th\$0 (108 numbers): q = B1 preset + b1 (16 hidden neurons) \, a = lrelu(q) = max(q \, 0.2 q) \, logit = B2 . a + b2 \, D = sigmoid(logit) = its belief that the preset is one of YOURS. Its 1761 parameters live in dp\$0: B1 (16 x 108 \, row by row) at 0 \, b1 at 1728 \, B2 at 1744 and b2 at 1760 - the logit ends up in lg\$0[0]., f 168;
#X obj 20 69 r \$0-critic;
#X obj 20 99 t b b b;
#X text 80 99 1) for every hidden neuron j: start with its bias b1_j \, add weight * input for all 108 inputs (row j of B1 starts at j * 108) \, store q_j - exactly what [nn.dense] does, f 64;
#X msg 80 156 16;
#X msg 120 156 0;
#X obj 80 182 until;
#X obj 80 208 f;
#X obj 120 208 + 1;
#X obj 80 236 t b b f;
#X obj 170 262 expr \$f1 \; \$f1 * 108 \; dp\$0[1728 + \$f1], f 64;
#X obj 170 322 v j_\$0;
#X obj 280 322 v jo_\$0;
#X obj 390 322 v acc_\$0;
#X obj 110 356 t b b;
#X msg 110 382 108;
#X msg 157 382 0;
#X obj 110 408 until;
#X obj 110 434 f;
#X obj 150 434 + 1;
#X obj 110 460 expr acc_\$0 + dp\$0[jo_\$0 + \$f1] * th\$0[\$f1], f 64;
#X obj 110 488 v acc_\$0;
#X obj 80 522 expr cq\$0[j_\$0] = acc_\$0, f 64;
#X obj 20 562 t b b;
#X text 80 562 2) the logit starts with the output bias b2, f 64;
#X obj 80 585 expr lg\$0[0] = dp\$0[1760], f 64;
#X obj 20 627 t b b b;
#X text 80 627 3) leaky ReLU a_j = max(q_j \, 0.2 q_j) \, and add B2_j * a_j to the logit, f 64;
#X msg 80 667 16;
#X msg 120 667 0;
#X obj 80 693 until;
#X obj 80 719 f;
#X obj 120 719 + 1;
#X obj 80 747 expr ca\$0[\$f1] = max(cq\$0[\$f1] \, 0.2 * cq\$0[\$f1]) \; lg\$0[0] = lg\$0[0] + dp\$0[1744 + \$f1] * max(cq\$0[\$f1] \, 0.2 * cq\$0[\$f1]), f 64;
